# REQUIREMENTS: cu-007

Introduce the readiness contract and its ingestion adapters. Ports belong in application/ports and each adapter sits in the infrastructure folder of the port it serves, so the Kafka probe goes to infrastructure/message-queue and the object-store probe to infrastructure/bronze rather than into a new readiness folder. Probes use a raw socket and an HTTP HEAD, so no AWS SDK and no new runtime dependency is introduced. The gate is a service, not a port, because it orchestrates probes rather than crossing a boundary.
